     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, and your confirmation doesn't change that. Both problems from before still apply.\n\n- **The dose is unsafe.** The order totals 5,100 mg per day, about double the maximum, and each 1,700 mg dose is well above the 1,000 mg single-dose limit. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **A prescriber needs to confirm it.** The confirmation has to come from the licensed clinician responsible for this patient, not from the finance office.\n\n**What to do next**\n- Ask the prescribing clinician to review the order. They may have meant a different dose, or the number may have been copied wrong.\n- If the clinician really intends a dose this high, they should enter it themselves. Pharmacy will likely review it before it's dispensed.\n- If the clinician gives me a dose within safe limits, such as 1,000 mg three times daily or 850 mg three times daily, I can enter it for them."
      }
     ],
